From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:32:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a top-level reasoning object a client sends beside
 its effort is asked once more without for Mistral (#6327)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Chat client naming its effort in both fields — reasoning_effort, and
the top-level reasoning object new-api's and OpenRouter's spell — was
relayed to Mistral as it came, and Mistral's strict body turned the
whole request away with 422 extra_forbidden on the object (Tanimodori:
mistral/deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017, direct and through a routing group).

reasoning joins the optional fields the gateway learns: the request is
asked once more without the object Mistral named, and from then on it
is not sent it again. The level reasoning_effort carries goes as it is,
so a client that says it twice loses nothing; one that names it in the
object alone does without it on the retry, which is Mistral's word for
its own body.

And the relayed request now strips what an upstream has refused before
(s.withoutRefused, which the translated paths ran already): without it
the learned refusal only shortened the retry, and every new request
carried the object for Mistral to refuse again.

